From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:57:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Engine: J714s on the 27.2 stub with a board Mach-O Stage
 1

The J714s (j714sap, T6050) moves from the 27.3 beta 1 stub and a raw Stage 1
to Apple's 27.2 (26B123) restore image and Aura's Mach-O boot object, the
way aurora-silicon boots M5 on 27.2: macOS 27.2 iBoot starts SPTM only for an
object with __TEXT_BOOT_EXEC (kcbz != 0), so Aura's object boots with SPTM
off, and Aura brings the secondary CPUs up inside the CTXR execute window.

- main.py (Engine/patches/0001): T6050 and j714sap minimum 27.2; the 27.3
  beta row is replaced by UniversalMac_27.2_26B123_Restore.ipsw, J714s iBoot
  mBoot-20457.41.3, RestoreLongVersion 26.2.123.0.0,0 (read from the IPSW's
  RestoreVersion.plist). The stub may be older than the system firmware, so a
  Mac on 27.2 or the 27.3 beta both take it.
- omarchy_macho.py (new): Aura's Mach-O boot object layout check and fill,
  ported from aurora-silicon/aurora-installer AuraStage1.swift
  (MachOBootObject, MIT): no __TEXT_BOOT_EXEC, every segment file-backed at
  its virtual offset, the raw image verbatim at the start of __TEXT_EXEC.
- omarchy_asahi.py: a board Mach-O contract (aurora_stage1 kind
  board-macho-ctxr-v1, BOARD_MACHO). For the J714s the template must name
  only j714sap, qualified on 27.2, and use the native Recovery app. Preflight
  checks esp/aurora/stage1-j714s.bin, esp/aurora/stage1-j714s.macho and
  esp/m1n1/boot-ctxr.bin before any disk change. Install fills the raw Stage 1
  (ESP PARTUUID, m1n1/boot-ctxr.bin), carries it into the boot object and
  hands it to Recovery staging. The 27.3 exact-candidate lock is removed.
- omarchy_recovery.py: a Mach-O mode: macho/aura-boot.macho (unpadded) and
  macho/boot-ctxr.bin, ESP path m1n1/boot-ctxr.bin, executeWindow 128 MiB.
  The native Recovery app pads and enrolls it.
- Tests for all of it; the common-raw-v1 system-firmware tests move to a
  neutral board.
- Engine renamed v0.9.2-omarchy.20261113.b25a51d6df57 and repacked from the
  authenticated engine.28 base: 17912434 bytes, sha256 bab38862...3f21, two
  identical repacks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
